  "slug": "inference-fit-6a61",
  "summary": "Six preprints test ML-based emulation, reconstruction and systematics mitigation for SKA, SPHEREx, kSZ, mm-wave and 21-cm analyses, with pipeline variability quantified.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the construction and stress-testing of inference components for upcoming surveys, with machine learning substituting for expensive or non-optimal steps. Vision Transformers outperform quadratic estimators in kSZ velocity reconstruction, and Wavelet-CFM generates jointly correlated lensing, kSZ, tSZ and CIB maps quickly. A differentiable GPU-accelerated hybrid forward model targets uncertainty quantification in global 21-cm inference, while symbolic regression diagnoses a Lyman-alpha flux power spectrum GP emulator, with a Sobolev loss improving derivative fidelity for most cases. SPHEREx work uses an information-criterion-driven non-linear deprojection of imaging systematics, tested on lognormal mocks. SKA SDC3b reports inter-team variability among 16 EoR pipelines, a reminder that validation across methods remains necessary. Not all items concern the same observable or method.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
